Multiply the numerators together and the denominators together:

\[
\frac{-5}{9}\cdot \frac{8}{17}
= \frac{(-5)(8)}{(9)(17)}
= \frac{-40}{153}
\]

Since \(40\) and \(153\) have no common factors other than \(1\), the fraction is already simplified.

\[
\boxed{-\frac{40}{153}}
\]

